/**
 * The connections catalog's marks (Whombat connections-catalog.md CX-01; app AP-760): the providers' own marks in their
 * own colours, drawn, never fetched (the strict CSP, offline boxes). Path data from Simple Icons 16.34.0 (CC0; the
 * Forgejo mark CC BY-SA 4.0, Caesar Schinas), unchanged geometry on a 24-unit box; trademarks stay their owners'.
 * Marks their owners publish in black (Notion, Tailscale) use `currentColor`, so they follow the text on a light or dark
 * tile. Proxmox Backup Server shows Proxmox's mark, UniFi Network and UniFi Protect Ubiquiti's.
 * Every catalog entry has a mark, so the apps always draw one (Whombat marks.md MK-02): Moneybird's from its website
 * (`moneybird-logo-mark-blue.svg`, even-odd holes, centred on a square box), Mollie's app icon (the white “m” of its
 * 2023 logo from docs.mollie.com on its black tile), the Model Context Protocol's (Simple Icons) for an MCP server, Gmail's
 * (Simple Icons) for Google mail, and for the two without a maker Lucide's (ISC) `sparkles` (an AI gateway) and `braces`
 * (an API), in `currentColor`.
 * Fusebox shows its own mark (John's own product, `assets/icon.svg`, Unlicense; AP-1127): the amber brackets and the fuse
 * between them, the fuse in `currentColor` the way Fusebox draws it light on dark and dark on light.
 * More connections (Whombat connections-more.md CM-28; app connections-more-web.md AP-2760): Plex, AdGuard, Pi-hole,
 * Nginx Proxy Manager, ESPHome, Pterodactyl, Airtable, HubSpot and Plausible from Simple Icons 16.35.0 (CC0), UniFi
 * Access Ubiquiti's like the other UniFi apps, TrueNAS the operating system's (`osMarks.ts`). Overseerr's own icon (MIT,
 * `public/os_icon.svg`: its disc and eye, the gradient drawn as the colour at its centre), Pipedrive's site mark (the
 * white “p” on its green circle). SABnzbd's and NZBHydra2's logos are GPL artwork, like MX Linux's (marks.md AP-2200), so
 * they get Lucide's `download` and `search`; Email (IMAP) Lucide's `mail`, the guide cards' envelope. A report tracker
 * (Whombat report-trackers.md) has no maker of its own: Lucide's `inbox`; a connection shows its driver's logo instead. Pterodactyl's navy
 * on its thin wings vanished on the dark theme, so it follows the text colour (AP-2774), as CentOS's does.
 * Synology DSM and QNAP (Whombat desk-found.md NS-01; app AP-3800): their wordmarks from Simple Icons 16.34.0 (CC0), both
 * in `currentColor` — Synology publishes its wordmark black (Simple Icons' grey faded on a light tile), QNAP's navy
 * vanished on the dark theme.
 * Sonarr and Radarr (Whombat service-dashboards.md SD-24, SD-S07; app service-dashboards.md AP-4570): in their own
 * colours. Simple Icons has neither; where their path data came from isn't recorded (`assets/marks/SOURCES.md`).
 * Overseerr's entry is shown as “Seerr” (CT-1009): Seerr carries Overseerr's disc and eye on, so the mark stays and
 * only its name changes.
 * GitHub Actions (Whombat service-dashboards.md “GitHub Actions”): Simple Icons 16.35.0 `githubactions` (CC0) in its blue.
 * T3 Code (Whombat t3code.md): the “T3” of its own logo (MIT, © 2026 T3 Tools Inc., `assets/prod/logo.svg`), white letters
 * on a black tile there; the letters alone in `currentColor` here, as GitHub's black mark, so they read on either theme.
 * Find My (docs/implementation/macos/findmy-connection.md) has a neutral mark of Whombat's own, drawn in Lucide's stroke:
 * a location pin over two people. Apple's Find My icon is never shown.
 * 1Password (Whombat onepassword-sync.md): Simple Icons 16.35.0 `1password` (CC0) in its blue.
 */
